{"purpose":"Capture the findings from the EKA migration/usage review: bugs, gaps, inconsistencies, and enhancements that would make EKA more usable for both programmers and agents.","content":"Findings from the migration review. Note two clarifications: (1) `eka get` is the machine interface and `eka view` is the human interface — same data, different output style; `view` intentionally has no --json. (2) The embedded FEEDBACK_ISSUE_TOKEN is deferred to a future security roadmap, not a work item now. The backlog covers: relationship flag override (silent data loss), --phase R7 bug, draft-to-draft reference tolerance, author identity placeholder, contentState transition gap, batch authoring, eka relate, workspace-native authoring, version-axis clarity, CLI polish, and release workflow_dispatch."}